  "title": "Erdős Problem #501",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For every $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$ let $A_x\\subset \\mathbb{R}$ be a bounded set with outer measure $<1$. Must there exist an infinite independent set, that is, some infinite $X\\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$ such that $x\not\\in A_y$ for all $x\neq y\\in X$?\nIf the sets $A_x$ are closed and have measure $<1$, then must there exist an independent set of size $3$?",
